ok - pins and floors are projected from their owners
ok - --pin tasks-axi refuses a pin below the floor or a pin the owner no longer defines
ok - a qualified profile passes and reports every tool
ok - a missing actionlint fails naming the owner action
ok - a non-pinned actionlint is a PINNED_MISMATCH
ok - suffixed shellcheck and actionlint builds are PINNED_MISMATCH exactly as the gates judge them
ok - a below-floor tasks-axi is refused
ok - a tasks-axi that advertises the pin but lacks a probed feature is refused
ok - --strict-pin catches a tasks-axi that drifted from the CI pin
ok - a node that reports a version but cannot execute .ts is CAPABILITY_MISSING
ok - node-ts is proved by executing a .ts file, not by the feature flag
ok - no-mistakes is always observed and required only on request
ok - an expected NM_HOME or PATH[0] that diverges is a PROFILE_MISMATCH
ok - a legacy-shaped login shell is reported as the legacy selection (negative control)
ok - --json carries the same verdict, rows, and typed lines
ok - unknown tools and arguments are usage errors
